# plans/plan_dx9.md D9-A5 scene corpus: skinned_quad
# The fourth non-BasicEffect Stock Effect, and the fifth (last) of the 5 XNA Stock Effects
# represented in the corpus: SkinnedEffect, on a brand-new vertex shape neither side had a
# built-in type for (PositionNormalTextureWeights: Position+Normal+TexCoord+BlendWeight+
# BlendIndices, stride 52 -- VSInputNmTxWeights, matches the existing stride-52 CNA vertex
# declaration byte-for-byte, D9-82f's own "no new vertex declaration needed" finding).
#
# Deliberately uses a SINGLE Identity bone at 100% vertex weight, the same simplification
# D9-82f's own DirectX9_DrawEx CTest used: skinning becomes a mathematical no-op, so the expected
# pixel math reduces to exactly the same lit-textured formula lit_textured_quad.scene already
# established (same dim light, same white texture, same (255,0,0)->(128,0,0)-style halving) --
# while still genuinely exercising the real per-vertex BLENDWEIGHT0/BLENDINDICES0 upload and the
# full Bones[72] register-upload path end to end, not skipped.
#
# weightspervertex=1 IS REQUIRED here, not merely omittable: real XNA's SkinnedEffect defaults
# WeightsPerVertex to 4 (confirmed in FNA's own SkinnedEffect.cs: `int weightsPerVertex = 4;`),
# matched by CNA's own SkinnedEffect.cpp default. A first version of this scene never set
# weightspervertex at all -- meaning it was ACTUALLY exercising the FourBones shader bucket the
# whole time despite this file's own original comment claiming "WeightsPerVertex=1" -- an
# undetected documentation error (the same category of mistake envmap_quad.scene's own
# fresnelfactor made), harmless here only because this vertex's weight[1..3] are all 0 (only one
# (boneindex,boneweight) pair is given per vertex line), which makes the extra bone terms
# structurally zero regardless of whether 1, 2, or 4 of them are actually summed by the shader.
# Explicitly setting weightspervertex=1 now makes this scene's own "single-bone" claim genuinely
# true and specifically exercises SkinnedEffect's OneBone shader bucket, distinct from the
# TwoBones/FourBones buckets. See skinned_twobone_quad.scene for a scene that actually exercises
# a genuine, non-degenerate 2-bone blend.
#
# SkinnedEffect implements IEffectLights.LightingEnabled via explicit interface implementation in
# real XNA/FNA too (same finding envmap_quad.scene's own header comment documents for
# EnvironmentMapEffect) -- lighting is always on, neither side sets it.
width=256
height=256
profile=HiDef
clearcolor=100,149,237,255
effect=SkinnedEffect
vertexformat=PositionNormalTextureWeights
lighting=true
ambientcolor=0,0,0
light0enabled=true
light0diffuse=0.5,0.5,0.5
light0direction=0,0,-1
texture=true
texturewidth=1
textureheight=1
texturefilter=Point
weightspervertex=1
primitive=TriangleList
texturepixel=255,255,255,255
# x,y,z,nx,ny,nz,u,v,boneindex,boneweight -- every vertex faces the camera (+Z normal), bound
# 100% to bone 0 (the single Identity bone both sides construct for this effect).
vertex=-0.6,0.6,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1.0
vertex=0.6,0.6,0,0,0,1,1,0,0,1.0
vertex=-0.6,-0.6,0,0,0,1,0,1,0,1.0
vertex=0.6,0.6,0,0,0,1,1,0,0,1.0
vertex=0.6,-0.6,0,0,0,1,1,1,0,1.0
vertex=-0.6,-0.6,0,0,0,1,0,1,0,1.0
